\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Amplitude sweep ($\Delta = \mathcal  {L}_{\text  {trained}}-\mathcal  {L}_{\text  {removed}}$, positive $=$ modulation harmful). Causal sensitivity grows with $\alpha $, but in the \emph  {destructive} direction: at $\alpha \geq 0.5$ the modulation makes the model worse, and $500$ further steps fail to reverse it. The $\alpha \approx 0.1$ regime---measurable structure with marginal, non-destructive function---is real but narrow.}}{8}{table.8}\protected@file@percent }
